      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not confident in this change - it seems to me that the current formula already computes ```total - prefixes_per_peer```, where ```prefixes_per_peer \u003d count_peer_count_many // bgp_peers_count```, I\u0027ve refactored it into that explicit two-step form in the patchset I am pushing now.\nAdditionally I verified againsyt a real run at ```count\u003d30000```, ```bgp_peers_count\u003d2```: each peer\u0027s log reports ```total_received_nlri_prefix_counter: 15000``` (30000 - 30000//2). The proposed ```count - (count // peers) // peers``` results in 22500, which wouldn\u0027t match the logged value, so the per-peer check would fail.\nAlso, on the robot: [line 121] is ```COUNT - COUNT // MULTIPLICITY``` (\u003d 300000 - 150000 \u003d 150000 for MULT\u003d2), and not ```COUNT - COUNT``` - the ```// MULTIPLICITY``` divides the subtracted term, so it\u0027s not always zero. \nThere is actually a #FIXME in there (line 132) that says that the value is only exact when ```COUNT``` is a multiple of ```MULTIPLICITY```, which we preserve (the count stays divisible by peer count).\n\nNot sure if I am missing something here though.",
